[{"id":111669,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/111669\">#1</a> I am preparing an entry for the <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Encyclopedia%20of%20Mathematical%20Physics%202nd%20ed\">Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics 2nd ed</a></em>:</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mtext> </mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span></span></span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Higher%20Topos%20Theory%20in%20Physics\">Higher Topos Theory in Physics</a></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mtext> </mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>Early draft now available at that link. </p>\n<p>Will be presenting this tomorrow at a CQTS-workshop on <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Center+for+Quantum+and+Topological+Systems#WorkshopOnHomotopyTheory2023\">Homotopy Theory and Applications</a></em>.</p>\n<p>Comments are welcome.</p>","timestamp":1697736708,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":111678,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/111678\">#2</a> Just a couple of typos for now:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>anlogous; Phsyics</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>And you have both ‘Snglr’ and ‘Snglrt’</p>","timestamp":1697798151,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":111679,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/111679\">#3</a> Thanks, fixed now.</p>\n<p>I want to say <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{Snglrt}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Snglrt</span></span></span></span></span> for the 2-category of <em>singulariTies</em> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">r</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">H</mi><mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">≔</mi></mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">t</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{Snglr}\\mathbf{H} \\coloneqq {\\mathrm{PSh}}_\\infty(\\mathbf{Snglrt, \\mathbf{H}})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Snglr</span></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">H</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mop\" style=\"position:relative;top:-0.0347em;\">:</span></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.0667em;\"></span></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">PSh</span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Snglrt</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">H</span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> for the <em>singular</em> version of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">H</span></span></span></span>.</p>","timestamp":1697799627,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":111681,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/111681\">#4</a> Second column of p.9, should that be <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">r</mi></mrow><mo>↪</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">d</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{Snglr} \\hookrightarrow \\mathbf{Grpd}_{\\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Snglr</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">↪</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9386em;vertical-align:-0.2441em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Grpd</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.0573em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4559em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2441em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>?</p>","timestamp":1697804452,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":111682,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/111682\">#5</a> Probably worth referencing a paper or two of your own, maybe <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Proper+Orbifold+Cohomology\">Proper Orbifold Cohomology</a>.</p>","timestamp":1697804922,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":111683,"sender_id":1037,"sender_full_name":"J-B Vienney","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/04c19b4b544f7d2de22328021eb01278?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/111683\">#6</a> I love this paper, thank you for writing it. Very helpful to get the main ideas of the field :)</p>","timestamp":1697809013,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":111686,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/111686\">#7</a> Thanks for the feedback. </p>\n<p>Just tried it as a presentation on an audience of topologists and mathematical physicists, and it seems to work well. Will post the video recording when it becomes available.</p>\n<p>(And I have added another remark that the document is in preparation and that references are (evidently?! :-) still missing.)</p>","timestamp":1697815132,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":117447,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/117447\">#8</a> Just saw a typo in (6), <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X&#x27;</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> should be <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Y</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">Y</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>Also, </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For further introduction to sheaf toposes see e.g. [Schreiber 2018] [Schapira 2023] and</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>looks like ‘and’ in the wrong place.</p>","timestamp":1727695654,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":117450,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/117450\">#9</a> Thanks! Fixed now (in the pdf <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Higher+Topos+Theory+in+Physics#download\">here</a>, still waiting for the galley proofs to make corrections there).</p>","timestamp":1727706361,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":117451,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/117451\">#10</a> A couple more:</p>\n<p>On p.4 in the line before </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In field theory this is the case for (Green-Schwarz type)…</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>presumably the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">p</span></span></span></span> should be <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n+2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span> in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">Ω</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{\\Omega}^p_{\\mathrm{dR}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0836em;vertical-align:-0.3013em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">Ω</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7823em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.3987em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathrm mtight\">dR</span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.1809em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3013em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>And there’s </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>wih</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>on p. 10.</p>","timestamp":1727712111,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":117452,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Higher.20Topos.20Theory.20in.20Physics/near/117452\">#11</a> Right. Thanks again! Fixed now.</p>","timestamp":1727712639,"subject":"Higher Topos Theory in Physics","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]